{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For</b>: This verse is joined to the one above, 'those who love Your name rejoice in You,' when they see that You drive away the wicked and bless the righteous." "<b>Some say</b> 'You crown him' is from the light [binyan], like 'they crown El David' [1 Chron. 12:19, i.e. 'crown David']. But the correct view is that it is from the increased [binyan], on the pattern of 'the king enriches him' [yeaʿashrehu], which means 'He enriches him' and goes out to two objects, and the true object is 'desire,' for the Holy One, blessed be He, crowns the righteous with desire. So the righteous is acted upon in part by the Holy One, blessed be He, for he is crowned with desire, but the desire itself is acted upon by Him alone in truth."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:22.522056818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}